 /**
+ * --nobuffer: DevTools keeps no copy of response bodies. With the Network domain enabled (Playwright
+ * enables it for every page, and this script enables it again for its own session) each agent buffers
+ * the body and decodes it on the page's main thread when the load finishes, for Network.getResponseBody:
+ * at 4x CPU that is about 70 ms for the 200-series body (3.4 MB), between the last byte and the page's
+ * next task, and no browser without DevTools open does it (design-system/reviews/chart-speed/PR.md).
+ * It reaches into Playwright's own session, which is not a public interface: a figure taken this way
+ * says so, and the default stays as it was.
+ */
+const NOBUFFER = process.argv.includes('--nobuffer')
+/**
